@startuml
title SHA3-256(M) : from message to digest
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
}

start
:Message M of any bit length;
:Append the 2-bit domain suffix 01\n(separates SHA-3 from SHAKE and from\noriginal Keccak, which appends nothing);
:Apply pad10*1 up to a multiple of\nthe rate, 1088 bits = 136 bytes;
note right
  First padding byte 0x06,
  last byte 0x80.
  A single padding byte is 0x86.
  Always at least 2 bits added.
end note
:Initialise the 1600-bit state to zero\nrate 1088 bits  +  capacity 512 bits;
while (another 136-byte block?) is (yes)
  :XOR the block into the rate;
  :Apply KECCAK-p[1600, 24]\n(24 rounds of theta, rho, pi, chi, iota);
endwhile (no)
:Read the first 256 bits of the rate;
:Digest, 32 bytes;
stop

note right
  Only one squeeze is needed:
  the 256-bit digest fits inside
  the 1088-bit rate.
  The 512-bit capacity is never
  read, which is why length
  extension does not apply.
end note
@enduml
